__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

.vercel
.env*

# Credentials the user CLI writes to disk.
#
# `npm run user add` and `npm run user token` deliberately write to a file
# rather than printing, so a password or token never lands in a terminal's
# scrollback. That is only half the job: the file is then sitting in the
# working tree, and a `git add -A` will happily commit it. This is that
# happening once, caught before the push.
#
# Delete these files once you have passed the credential on.
*-watcher-token.txt
*-password.txt

# Working files that a stray `git add -A` must never sweep into a public repo.
# vault-owner.json in particular holds the vault side of the bridge.
vault-owner.json
probe-stores.json
dna-card-vault-ro/
ship.ps1
commitmsg.txt
